  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Governance Foundation Phase II.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia Governance Foundation Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute towards an accountable and responsive government working with active citizens to satisfactorily implement pro-poor policies.

The ZGF provided comprehensive grants and capacity development support to Zambian civil society organisations (CSOs) in all 10 of the country&apos;s provinces. The organisation was supported through a basket funding arrangement known as the Joint Financing Agreement (JFA) with contributions from the Department for International Development (DFID), Danish International Development Agency (DANIDA), Irish Aid, Swedish International Development Agency (Sida) and Deutsche Gesellschaft fr Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZGF is a re-granting institution providing financial support and      capacity building for civil society organisations in Zambia. ZGF&apos;s    partners are both well-established and, increasingly so, smaller      organisations and groupings who can grow stronger and more            professional with the support of ZGF. With its support of 80 MSEK     over three years Sweden is the biggest cooperating partner.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ZGF vidaref&#xf6;rmedlar medel till organisationer i det civila samh&#xe4;llet  och tillhandah&#xe5;ller kapacitetsutveckling kring organisatorisk oc      finansiell styrning samt i de &#xe4;mnen som organisationerna sj&#xe4;lva       efterfr&#xe5;gar st&#xf6;d i. Bland ZGF:s partner finns etablerade              organisationer och mindre organisationer och grupper som med ZGF:s    st&#xf6;d kan v&#xe4;xa sig starkare och mer professionella.</narrative>
  </description>
